SOAPBOX: It was a great contest! Bands were widely opened, The signals were overloading the receiver. This was my first experience in the Low Power category, using a homebrew 50W amplifier built with inexpensive MOSFETs—it was far more engaging than my previous QRP experiences. Unfortunately, due to Russian shelling, the region is facing electricity shortages and frequent power outages as a result, I had to operate off a car battery at reduced power for nearly half the time. Thanks to all the participants and organizers for this fantastic event!
